---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE.name} Kids' Printables`} description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your information. Names typed into our worksheet tools never leave your device.`}>
  <article class="prose-tl mx-auto max-w-[68ch] px-4 sm:px-6 pt-12">
    <h1 class="text-[2.2rem] font-bold"><span class="ruled">Privacy</span></h1>
    <p class="mt-6"><em>Draft for legal review. Last updated October 4, 2026.</em></p>
    <p>{SITE.name} is made for adults: parents, teachers and homeschool families. Children are not meant to use the site directly, and we don't offer accounts for children.</p>
    <h2>Names you type</h2>
    <p>Our worksheet tools run entirely in your web browser. When you type a name, the worksheet and its PDF are created on your device. The name is not sent to our servers, not stored by us, and not shared with anyone.</p>
    <h2>Your email address</h2>
    <p>If you give us your email, to keep downloading or to join the membership waitlist, we add it to our private email list (kept in a spreadsheet only we can see, or with an email service such as Kit) to send you new printables and membership news. We never ask for, and never store, a child's name or details alongside it. You can unsubscribe from any email, or ask us to delete your address anytime.</p>
    <h2>Members and payments</h2>
    <p>If you become a member, payment is handled by Square. Your card details go straight to Square and never reach our servers. Square shares with us your name, email, the last 4 digits of your card and your subscription status, so we can switch on member features and let you sign in. Square's own privacy notice covers how it handles your payment information.</p>
    <p>When you sign in as a member, we set one cookie that keeps you signed in on that browser for up to 60 days. It holds only your email and your Square customer reference, and it's signed so it can't be altered. Signing out removes it.</p>
    <h2>What else we collect</h2>
    <p>We use two analytics tools to see which pages people visit, so we know what to improve. Vercel Web Analytics counts visits without cookies. Google Analytics uses cookies to count visits and see how people move around the site, such as which pages they view, roughly where they are (country or city), and what kind of device they use. We've turned off Google's advertising features and Google signals, so this data isn't used to show you ads. You can opt out of Google Analytics with Google's <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">browser add-on</a> or by blocking cookies.</p>
    <p>When a PDF is downloaded, we also get a private notification saying which page it came from, how many pages it was and the approximate city, so we know the tools are being used. It never includes the file name or anything you typed. Analytics never sees the names you type into our tools. Names stay in your browser and are never put in page addresses or sent to us. We don't use advertising trackers or ad pixels anywhere on the site.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
